AWS ECS Fargate Deployment: Nautilus Application
This project documents the containerization and deployment of a web application onto Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS) using the Fargate serverless launch type, managed via the AWS CLI in the us-east-1 region.

Architecture Overview
[ Dockerfile (/root/pyapp) ]
           │
           ▼ (Build & Tag)
   [ Amazon ECR ] (nautilus-ecr)
           │
           ▼ (Task Definition)
[ ECS Cluster ] (nautilus-cluster)
           │
           ▼ (Fargate Service & ENI)
[ Public Internet ] ──(Port 80)──► [ Nginx Web App ]
Deployment Steps & Commands
1. Authenticate Docker to ECR and Create Repository
Bash
export AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1

# Authenticate Docker client with Amazon ECR
aws ecr get-login-password --region us-east-1 | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 915322164324.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com

# Create a private ECR repository
aws ecr create-repository --repository-name nautilus-ecr --region us-east-1
2. Build, Tag, and Push the Docker Image
Bash
cd /root/pyapp

# Build the container image from the local Dockerfile
docker build -t nautilus-ecr .

# Tag the image for your ECR registry
docker tag nautilus-ecr:latest 915322164324.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/nautilus-ecr:latest

# Push the image to ECR
docker push 915322164324.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/nautilus-ecr:latest
3. Create the ECS Cluster and Register the Task Definition
Bash
# Create an ECS cluster using Fargate
aws ecs create-cluster --cluster-name nautilus-cluster --region us-east-1

# Create the task definition JSON configuration
cat << 'EOF' > task-def.json
{
  "family": "nautilus-taskdefinition",
  "networkMode": "awsvpc",
  "requiresCompatibilities": [
    "FARGATE"
  ],
  "cpu": "256",
  "memory": "512",
  "executionRoleArn": "arn:aws:iam::915322164324:role/ecsTaskExecutionRole",
  "containerDefinitions": [
    {
      "name": "pyapp",
      "image": "915322164324.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/nautilus-ecr:latest", 
      "essential": true,
      "portMappings": [
        {
          "containerPort": 80,
          "hostPort": 80,
          "protocol": "tcp"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
EOF

# Register the task definition with ECS
aws ecs register-task-definition --cli-input-json file://task-def.json --region us-east-1
4. Create and Run the ECS Fargate Service
Bash
# Fetch default subnet and security group IDs
SUBNET_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-subnets --filters "Name=defaultForAz,Values=true" --query "Subnets[0].SubnetId" --output text --region us-east-1)
SG_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-security-groups --filters "Name=group-name,Values=default" --query "SecurityGroups[0].GroupId" --output text --region us-east-1)

# Create the ECS service to run the task on Fargate
aws ecs create-service \
  --cluster nautilus-cluster \
  --service-name nautilus-service \
  --task-definition nautilus-taskdefinition \
  --desired-count 1 \
  --launch-type FARGATE \
  --network-configuration "awsvpcConfiguration={subnets=[$SUBNET_ID],securityGroups=[$SG_ID],assignPublicIp=ENABLED}" \
  --region us-east-1
5. Configure Network Access & Security Groups
To allow public HTTP traffic access to the Fargate container task, authorize inbound traffic on port 80 for the associated security group:

Bash
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
  --group-id sg-0ed84da4510ad2a9d \
  --protocol tcp \
  --port 80 \
  --cidr 0.0.0.0/0 \
  --region us-east-1
Verification
Test connection to the running Fargate task's Public IP:

Bash
curl -I http://<TASK_PUBLIC_IP>
